  "Specification": "This module provides a TLAPS proof for the InternalMemory specification, specifically proving that the type invariant (TypeInvariant) is preserved by the system. The proof addresses the fact that TypeInvariant alone is not inductive due to the way the next-state action Do(p) accesses fields of buf[p], which are only valid when buf[p] is in MReq. To resolve this, the invariant is strengthened with BufConsistent, which ensures that buf[p] has the correct type depending on the value of ctl[p]. The main theorem proved is that ISpec implies []TypeInvariant, using the strengthened invariant Inv (TypeInvariant /\\ BufConsistent). The proof is structured hierarchically and uses TLAPS proof commands and backend solvers.",
